ing hops 639->528, 639->1818, 1688->528, 595->528, 528->1186, 1818->1186 all exist (steps_14-21, 25-27). However, every tool available in this session aggregates over the entire 0-100000 horizon; none returns timestamps or restricts to [61549, 99948]. I therefore cannot verify the defining requirement - that consecutive hops occur in increasing time order with gaps of at most 600 units - so a time-respecting cascade can be neither confirmed nor refuted from the evidence obtainable here. Confounder controls argue against uncritically accepting the static path: all mediators are among the graph's busiest nodes (639: 486 events/353 partners, 595: 418, 1688: 375, 528: 182; steps_12, 13), and they sit in thousands of triangles (639: 2053, 1688: 1475, 528: 525; step_23), so 1385 and 1186 would appear statically 'connected' through them regardless of any influence flow - note 1186 itself is in zero triangles. Moreover each candidate hop fired exactly once, with no repetition (repeat_ratio 0.0531 overall, step_01), so a cascade would require several one-shot events to land within 600 units by coincidence; the rough chance alignment for a two-hop chain in this ~38.4k window is ~2.4e-4, and ~1e-3 across the four candidate routes (steps_24, 28). That low base rate leans toward 'absent', but without any timestamp access the honest verdict is insufficient evidence."}, "raw_final_response": "```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_8980b60f\",\n  \"decision\": \"insufficient\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [1385, 1186, 639, 595, 1688, 528, 1818, 1259],\n  \"window\": [61549, 99948],\n  \"confidence\": 0.6,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_17\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_16\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_18\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_19\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_20\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_21\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_25\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_26\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_27\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_23\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_24\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_28\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"There is no direct 1385->1186 edge (step_17). Static two-hop routes do exist: 1385 reaches 639, 595 and 1688 (step_03), 1186 is reached only from 528, 1259 and 1818 (step_04), and the connecting hops 639->528, 639->1818, 1688->528, 595->528, 528->1186, 1818->1186 all exist (steps_14-21, 25-27). However, every tool available in this session aggregates over the entire 0-100000 horizon; none returns timestamps or restricts to [61549, 99948]. I therefore cannot verify the defining requirement - that consecutive hops occur in increasing time order with gaps of at most 600 units - so a time-respecting cascade can be neither confirmed nor refuted from the evidence obtainable here. Confounder controls argue against uncritically accepting the static path: all mediators are among the graph's busiest nodes (639: 486 events/353 partners, 595: 418, 1688: 375, 528: 182; steps_12, 13), and they sit in thousands of triangles (639: 2053, 1688: 1475, 528: 525; step_23), so 1385 and 1186 would appear statically 'connected' through them regardless of any influence flow - note 1186 itself is in zero triangles. Moreover each candidate hop fired exactly once, with no repetition (rep